in this video I'm gonna show you how to  get your MacBook Air to stop running so  loud well it's constantly trying to keep  itself from overheating and these  solutions are not gonna be like my  previous ones where I water-cooled it  and I use the gel pack these are gonna  be safe permanent solutions these tips  actually apply to most Macs made within  the last few years and as a bonus you're  most likely going to gain a few extra  hours of battery life as well like most  people I was extremely excited for the  new MacBook Air that's because we have a  new keyboard that other than this laptop  it's only available in a 16 inch MacBook  Pro which is much larger heavier and  more expensive we also have twice the  SSD capacity and we have new Intel CPUs  that offer twice the cores and with  better graphics giving us much more  performance for the same price because  of this many people are choosing to go  with the new MacBook Air instead of a  pro which costs more money but there's  only one problem  Apple did not put in a good cooler into  the system which means it runs hotter  and louder now if it only did that  during super difficult tasks that might  be fine but I'm seeing this in normal  use as well for example when I open  Chrome and went to youtube and scroll  down the air hit a hundred degrees  Celsius if you have a few tabs open and  you quickly flip between them it  actually hits a hundred degrees Celsius  and then I ended up watching as 4k 60  video and not only did the MacBook Air  hit a hundred degrees Celsius within  about 10 seconds  the fans sped up to about 6,000 rpm  which is annoying and it just stay there  now I know that not that many of you are  gonna be watching 4k video on your  MacBook Air so I tested out 1080p 60  video and it still ran really hot at 90  degrees Celsius but thankfully the fans  were spinning lower my first tip is  simple  don't use Chrome now Chrome is my  favorite browser but unfortunately it is  much more Hardware intensive thus that  means you get more heat Safari on the  other hand focuses on efficiency and  that same 1080p 60 video playback at 65  degrees Celsius with the fan completely  off opening YouTube and quickly  scrolling down I hit a max of 86 degrees  Celsius instead of a hundred and then  quickly jumping through tops for twice  as long  I couldn't get it to hit over 67 degrees  Celsius instead of quickly hitting 100  so if you're not picky about web  browsers definitely use Safari but what  if you are or what if you're running  other apps or doing other things and  your MacBook Air is running hot and loud  for example what if you want to do some  light photo or video editing or what if  you're running a dedicated app for video  streaming or even downloading and  installing files and your fan is going  crazy this is where the MacBook Air  started to kill me I was playing back a  game trailer in the epic games app and  the CPU was hitting a hundred degrees  Celsius what the fan spinning up but not  being too annoying and then I started  downloading and installing for night and  at that point after about a minute the  fan was running a full blast the CPU is  at a hundred degrees Celsius and it  stayed this way for over an hour while I  downloaded the game this is absolutely  ridiculous and let me explain why this  is happening and then tell you how you  guys can help with this issue the way  until designs their CPUs especially in  the last couple of years your processor  can actually use more than double the  wattage in certain cases to get it to  run faster for example this 1.1  gigahertz processor can actually hit up  to 3.5 gigahertz and this does make this  new MacBook Air very snappy and very  quick in fact snappier than my macbook  pro but because of that it uses more  power and puts out more heat now this  isn't a bad thing by itself but when you  pair turbo boost with a poor cooling  design and apps that are very processor  and graphics intensive that leads to  this MacBook Air running hotter and  louder than a MacBook Pro now the other  reason why is that Mac OS will give you  the maximum amount of performance when  an application asks for it because  unlike Windows there are no power  options so it doesn't default in power  efficiency or balance mode so if you're  doing something that could be sped up  with more CPU or graphics power it will  actually give it as much as I can even  if that means running hot and loud you  can see in our Cinebench are 20 tests  that the MacBook Air is trying to run  the CPU as fast as possible even though  we're at a hundred resale seus and the  fans are going at almost full blast this  is where turbo boost switcher comes in  and that's a third-party app that will  turn off turbo boost and we'll stop the  CPU from trying to reach those crazy  high frequencies even when the laptop  doesn't need it  let's start off with the free version I  downloaded it installed it allowed it to  run into security settings and then  restarted and then I went ahead and  turned off turbo boost  I opened up YouTube in Chrome and then  quickly scroll down and attempts only  hit 64 degrees Celsius instead of a  hundred I then played back a 4k 60 video  which is quite demanding and the laptop  maxed out at 85 degrees Celsius and with  the fan running at its slowest speed  possible instead of a hundred degrees  running at over five thousand rpm after  a few minutes of playing back trailers  in the epic games app the CPU did not  peak above 75 degrees Celsius and the  fan was silent as soon as I turn off  turbo boost switcher you can see that  our CPU goes from China run as fast as  possible and hitting a hundred three  Celsius to running at a constant 1.1  gigahertz  with a steady decline in temps and fan  speeds resulting with a maximum  temperature of 85 degrees Celsius and a  laptop staying completely silent now  since we are limiting the power that  also means that we're limiting the  performance which is a big bummer on a  brand new powerful machine thankfully  for normal uses I didn't really notice a  difference in performance it still felt  noticeably snappier than the 2019 air  Google Chrome was still responsive when  jumping through tabs and scrolling and  even 4k 60 video playback fine the whole  system is quick and responsive and since  the CPU isn't having these massive  wattage spikes that means that you are  gonna gain a few hours of battery life I  did notice some difference in  performances with apps that need a lot  more power so I decided to rerun  Cinebench R 20 it definitely took longer  but the CPU didn't ever go higher than  70 degrees Celsius and the fan ran  silent at its lowest speed instead of  being loud and hitting 100 degrees  Celsius the end result was a score of  630 and set of 955 which is a noticeable  drop in performance putting it very  close to 2019 macbook air but keep in  mind the 2019 air has to run hot and  loud to achieve those levels of  performance  we're the new one wit turbo boost off  can do so while running completely  silent really cool and at the same time  using less power my last tip would be to  buy turbo boost switcher pro for only  $10 this will allow you to schedule when  to have turbo boost on or off or allow  it to toggle based on the app if you  have a few apps that always make your  macbook air run hot that way you can  maximize your temperature to performance  ratio of course I wish that Apple not  only upgraded the specs and the  performance of this MacBook Air but  actually put in a decent cooler into the  machine that would have made it amazing  and unfortunately they didn't and it  kind of sucks having to use third-party  software and limiting performance to get  good thermals that definitely is a  bummer but until Apple comes out with  some kind of power modes like Windows  has which also lowers your performance  but gives you better battery life and  you know less heat this is what we're  gonna have to result to doing or maybe  just wait for a MacBook Air that has a  much better cooler so thank you guys for  watching if you have any questions ask  in the comments section down below I'll  have a link to turbo boost switcher in  the video description it's not affiliate  link or anything like that I just really  like the program if you guys want to see  more videos like this one especially our  full review of the MacBook Air you guys  can click that circle above and check  out one of those two great videos right  over there this max and I'll see you in  the next video  [Music]

